}

Enable the BigInt type. See how to enable it in Use BigInt type to represent Kotlin's Long type .","title":"Use Kotlin code from JavaScript","source":"https://kotlinlang.org/docs/js-to-kotlin-interop.html","sections":["Use Kotlin code from JavaScript > Package structure > Use BigInt type to represent Kotlin's Long type > Use Long in exported declarations"],"line_start":264,"line_end":282,"score":0.463117778301239,"release_version":null,"availability":"unknown"},{"anchor":"property-names","start":7712,"end":8376,"split_code":false,"platforms":["common"],"id":"54c225497944b0ee3c77f7504844e98a18dda271d4450c0923a4a977726e03fb","document_id":"coding-conventions","strategy":"semantic","text":"Property names

Names of constants (properties marked with const , or top-level or object val properties with no custom get function that hold deeply immutable data) should use all uppercase, underscore-separated names following the screaming snake case convention:

