@JsName("new C()")   // error here
external fun newC()","title":"Use Kotlin code from JavaScript","source":"https://kotlinlang.org/docs/js-to-kotlin-interop.html","sections":["Use Kotlin code from JavaScript > Package structure > @JsName annotation"],"line_start":66,"line_end":77,"score":0.5161665678024292,"release_version":null,"availability":"unknown"},{"anchor":"support-for-jsexport-in-multiplatform-expect-declarations","start":32544,"end":32928,"split_code":false,"platforms":["common","jvm","android","native","js","wasm"],"id":"3f6fb55f0e1f578e9d943aabb52ddaa24f4f6ecc55251ac8bc407c95eb9b0e99","document_id":"whatsnew22","strategy":"semantic","text":"You must also annotate with @JsExport the corresponding actual implementation in the JavaScript source set, and it has to use only exportable types.

