    fun hello() {
        println("Hello $name!")
    }

    @JsName("helloWithGreeting")
    fun hello(greeting: String) {
        println("$greeting $name!")
    }
}

Now you can use this class from JavaScript in the following way:

// If necessary, import 'kjs' according to chosen module system
var person = new kjs.Person("Dmitry");   // refers to module 'kjs'
person.hello();                          // prints "Hello Dmitry!"
person.helloWithGreeting("Servus");      // prints "Servus Dmitry!"","title":"Use Kotlin code from JavaScript","source":"https://kotlinlang.org/docs/js-to-kotlin-interop.html","sections":["Use Kotlin code from JavaScript > Package structure > @JsName annotation"],"line_start":43,"line_end":64,"score":0.537909984588623,"release_version":null,"availability":"unknown"},{"anchor":"kotlin-types-in-javascript","start":11040,"end":12567,"split_code":false,"platforms":["js"],"id":"1fac1580adb5a57b3a137a078c51e7a03cc01260ebb05bc534d79cd6957a4be7","document_id":"js-to-kotlin-interop","strategy":"semantic","text":"Kotlin types in JavaScript

