{"question":"How should I handle undefined or null when calling an external JavaScript function?","candidates":[{"anchor":"declare-parameters-with-default-values","start":3296,"end":3902,"split_code":false,"platforms":["js"],"id":"712359572c81b236f5c6335f575dd71d78b687a5a7fae28ff9f33488260e6d33","document_id":"js-interop","strategy":"semantic","text":"Declare parameters with default values

If you are writing an external declaration for a JavaScript function which has a parameter with a default value, use definedExternally . This delegates the generation of the default values to the JavaScript function itself:

external fun myFunWithOptionalArgs(
    x: Int,
    y: String = definedExternally,
    z: String = definedExternally
)

With this external declaration, you can call myFunWithOptionalArgs with one required argument and two optional arguments, where the default values are calculated by the JavaScript implementation of myFunWithOptionalArgs .","title":"Use JavaScript code from Kotlin","source":"https://kotlinlang.org/docs/js-interop.html","sections":["Use JavaScript code from Kotlin > external modifier > Declare parameters with default values"],"line_start":87,"line_end":97,"score":0.5613446831703186,"release_version":null,"availability":"unknown"},{"anchor":"external-modifier","start":1592,"end":2598,"split_code":false,"platforms":["js"],"id":"ea1bb45f19d675790de3284d7eebb628497bbd4954c59494aa2d1330f9aadb36","document_id":"js-interop","strategy":"semantic","text":"external modifier

To tell Kotlin that a certain declaration is written in pure JavaScript, you should mark it with the external modifier. When the compiler sees such a declaration, it assumes that the implementation for the corresponding class, function or property is provided externally (by the developer or via an npm dependency ), and therefore does not try to generate any JavaScript code from the declaration. This is also why external declarations can't have a body. For example:

external fun alert(message: Any?): Unit

external class Node {
    val firstChild: Node

    fun append(child: Node): Node

    fun removeChild(child: Node): Node

    // etc
}

