                }
            }
        }
    }
}","title":"What's new in Kotlin 2.4.20","source":"https://kotlinlang.org/docs/whatsnew2420.html","sections":["What's new in Kotlin 2.4.20 > Kotlin/JS > Support for exporting suspending lambdas as async functions"],"line_start":505,"line_end":523,"score":0.40259069204330444,"release_version":"2.4.20","availability":"See individual feature status in source; release version is not a snippet compatibility guarantee."},{"anchor":"new-export-of-suspend-function-with-jsexport","start":18558,"end":18655,"split_code":false,"platforms":["common","jvm","android","native","js","wasm"],"id":"8e56bf8998dcf00edb75ac5b237b79a15d3e4830a5a6adbf80b1f81532b45344","document_id":"whatsnew23","strategy":"semantic","text":"This feature is Experimental . We would appreciate your feedback in our issue tracker, YouTrack .","title":"What's new in Kotlin 2.3.0","source":"https://kotlinlang.org/docs/whatsnew23.html","sections":["What's new in Kotlin 2.3.0 > Kotlin/JS > New export of suspend function with JsExport"],"line_start":427,"line_end":427,"score":0.40131875872612,"release_version":"2.3.0","availability":"See individual feature status in source; release version is not a snippet compatibility guarantee."},{"anchor":"provide-documentation-with-kdoc-comments","start":4176,"end":5288,"split_code":false,"platforms":["native"],"id":"40d87ddc3788a24a4cf86a971a5b7252c8b08dc065ae0f678b4e07c9ae83589f","document_id":"native-objc-interop","strategy":"semantic","text":"KDoc comments are embedded into klibs and extracted from klibs into the produced Apple frameworks. As a result, comments on classes and methods appear during autocompletion, for example in Xcode. If you go to the definition of functions in the .h file, you'll see comments on @param , @return , and similar tags.

Known limitations:

Dependency documentation is not exported unless it is compiled with the -Xexport-kdoc option. Libraries compiled with this compiler option might be incompatible with other compiler versions.

